  "c5x-s33": { name: "The graph of f'", label: "Graph", intro: String.raw`The function $f$ is differentiable on the closed interval $[-4, 4]$. The graph of its derivative $f'$, which consists of line segments, is shown below.`, sources: [{ title: "", blocks: [{ svg: graph({ x: [-4, 4], y: [-4, 4], xname: "x", yname: "y", segments: [[-4, 2, -3, 0], [-3, 0, -2, 2], [-2, 2, -1, 3], [-1, 3, 2, 0], [2, 0, 4, 2]], dots: [[-4, 2, "closed"], [4, 2, "closed"]], alt: "Graph of the derivative f prime for x from -4 to 4, made of line segments joining the points (-4, 2), (-3, 0), (-2, 2), (-1, 3), (2, 0), (4, 2). It touches the x-axis without crossing at x = -3 and x = 2." }) }] }] },
  "c5x-s34": { name: "A velocity graph", label: "Graph", intro: String.raw`A particle moves along the $x$-axis. The graph of its velocity $v(t)$, for $0 \le t \le 7$, consists of line segments and is shown below.`, sources: [{ title: "", blocks: [{ svg: graph({ x: [0, 7], y: [-4, 4], xname: "t", yname: "y", segments: [[0, 2, 3, -1], [3, -1, 4, -3], [4, -3, 5, -1], [5, -1, 7, 1]], dots: [[0, 2, "closed"], [7, 1, "closed"]], alt: "Graph of the velocity v for t from 0 to 7, made of line segments joining the points (0, 2), (3, -1), (4, -3), (5, -1), (7, 1). It crosses the t-axis at t = 2 and t = 6." }) }] }] },
  "c5x-s35": { name: "The graph of f'", label: "Graph", intro: String.raw`The function $f$ is differentiable on the closed interval $[-3, 4]$. The graph of its derivative $f'$, which consists of line segments, is shown below.`, sources: [{ title: "", blocks: [{ svg: graph({ x: [-3, 4], y: [-4, 4], xname: "x", yname: "y", segments: [[-3, -3, -2, -2], [-2, -2, 0, 2], [0, 2, 2, -2], [2, -2, 3, 0], [3, 0, 4, -1]], dots: [[-3, -3, "closed"], [4, -1, "closed"]], alt: "Graph of the derivative f prime for x from -3 to 4, made of line segments joining the points (-3, -3), (-2, -2), (0, 2), (2, -2), (3, 0), (4, -1). It crosses the x-axis at x = -1 and x = 1. It touches the x-axis without crossing at x = 3." }) }] }] },
  "c5x-s36": { name: "Values of f'", label: "Table", intro: String.raw`The function $f$ has a continuous derivative. Selected values of $f'$ are given in the table below.`, sources: [{ title: "", blocks: [{ table: { head: [String.raw`$x$`, String.raw`$-2$`, String.raw`$-1$`, String.raw`$0$`, String.raw`$1$`, String.raw`$2$`, String.raw`$3$`], rows: [[String.raw`$f'(x)$`, String.raw`$2$`, String.raw`$-3$`, String.raw`$4$`, String.raw`$-1$`, String.raw`$-3$`, String.raw`$-3$`]] } }] }] },
  "c5x-s37": { name: "The graph of f'", label: "Graph", intro: String.raw`The function $f$ is differentiable on the closed interval $[-2, 5]$. The graph of its derivative $f'$, which consists of line segments, is shown below.`, sources: [{ title: "", blocks: [{ svg: graph({ x: [-2, 5], y: [-4, 4], xname: "x", yname: "y", segments: [[-2, -2, -1, 0], [-1, 0, 2, -3], [2, -3, 4, -1], [4, -1, 5, -2]], dots: [[-2, -2, "closed"], [5, -2, "closed"]], alt: "Graph of the derivative f prime for x from -2 to 5, made of line segments joining the points (-2, -2), (-1, 0), (2, -3), (4, -1), (5, -2). It touches the x-axis without crossing at x = -1." }) }] }] },
  "c5x-s38": { name: "A velocity graph", label: "Graph", intro: String.raw`A particle moves along the $x$-axis. The graph of its velocity $v(t)$, for $0 \le t \le 7$, consists of line segments and is shown below.`, sources: [{ title: "", blocks: [{ svg: graph({ x: [0, 7], y: [-4, 4], xname: "t", yname: "y", segments: [[0, 2, 2, -2], [2, -2, 4, 2], [4, 2, 6, -2], [6, -2, 7, -3]], dots: [[0, 2, "closed"], [7, -3, "closed"]], alt: "Graph of the velocity v for t from 0 to 7, made of line segments joining the points (0, 2), (2, -2), (4, 2), (6, -2), (7, -3). It crosses the t-axis at t = 1 and t = 3 and t = 5." }) }] }] },
  "c5x-s39": { name: "The graph of f'", label: "Graph", intro: String.raw`The function $f$ is differentiable on the closed interval $[-2, 5]$. The graph of its derivative $f'$, which consists of line segments, is shown below.`, sources: [{ title: "", blocks: [{ svg: graph({ x: [-2, 5], y: [-4, 4], xname: "x", yname: "y", segments: [[-2, -2, -1, -3], [-1, -3, 1, -1], [1, -1, 2, -2], [2, -2, 3, 0], [3, 0, 5, -2]], dots: [[-2, -2, "closed"], [5, -2, "closed"]], alt: "Graph of the derivative f prime for x from -2 to 5, made of line segments joining the points (-2, -2), (-1, -3), (1, -1), (2, -2), (3, 0), (5, -2). It touches the x-axis without crossing at x = 3." }) }] }] },
  "c5x-s40": { name: "A drone's height", label: "Graph", intro: String.raw`A drone takes off from a ledge below the edge of a cliff. Its height $h(t)$, in meters above the edge of the cliff, $t$ seconds after takeoff is shown below for $0 \le t \le 8$. $h$ is differentiable.`, sources: [{ title: "", blocks: [{ svg: graph({ x: [0, 8], y: [-6, 10], step: { x: 1, y: 2 }, xname: "t", yname: "h", fns: [{ f: (x) => 8 - 0.5 * (x - 5) ** 2, from: 0, to: 8 }], dots: [[5, 8, "closed"]], alt: "Graph of the height h, in meters above the edge of a cliff, against time t in seconds, for t from 0 to 8. The graph is a downward-opening parabola that starts at (0, -4.5), crosses the t-axis at t = 1, reaches its highest point at (5, 8), and then falls to (8, 3.5)." }) }] }] },
  "c5x-s41": { name: "Revenue and price", label: "Table", intro: String.raw`A store's weekly revenue $R(p)$, in dollars, depends on the price $p$, in dollars, it charges for a product. $R$ is twice differentiable and $R''(p) < 0$ for all $p$. Selected values of $R'(p)$ are given in the table below.`, sources: [{ title: "", blocks: [{ table: { head: [String.raw`$p$`, String.raw`$4$`, String.raw`$6$`, String.raw`$8$`, String.raw`$10$`, String.raw`$12$`], rows: [[String.raw`$R'(p)$`, String.raw`$15$`, String.raw`$9$`, String.raw`$6$`, String.raw`$-4$`, String.raw`$-11$`]] } }] }] },
  "c5x-s42": { name: "A rectangle in a triangle", label: "Diagram", intro: String.raw`A rectangle has its base on the $x$-axis and its two upper corners on the sides of the triangle with vertices $(-3, 0)$, $(3, 0)$, and $(0, 4)$, as shown below. The upper right corner is $(x, y)$.`, sources: [{ title: "", blocks: [{ svg: graph({ x: [-4, 4], y: [0, 5], xname: "x", yname: "y", segments: [[-3, 0, 0, 4], [0, 4, 3, 0], [-1.0, 0, -1.0, 2.6666666666666665], [-1.0, 2.6666666666666665, 1.0, 2.6666666666666665], [1.0, 2.6666666666666665, 1.0, 0]], dots: [[1.0, 2.6666666666666665, "closed"]], labels: [[1.2, 2.9666666666666663, "(x, y)"]], alt: "An isosceles triangle with base from (-3, 0) to (3, 0) on the x-axis and top vertex at (0, 4). A rectangle stands on the base, centered on the y-axis, with its two upper corners on the slanted sides; the upper right corner is labeled (x, y)." }) }] }] },
  "c5x-s43": { name: "A drone's height", label: "Graph", intro: String.raw`A drone takes off from a ledge below the edge of a cliff. Its height $h(t)$, in meters above the edge of the cliff, $t$ seconds after takeoff is shown below for $0 \le t \le 8$. $h$ is differentiable.`, sources: [{ title: "", blocks: [{ svg: graph({ x: [0, 8], y: [-10, 11], step: { x: 1, y: 2 }, xname: "t", yname: "h", fns: [{ f: (x) => 9 - 1.0 * (x - 4) ** 2, from: 0, to: 8 }], dots: [[4, 9, "closed"]], alt: "Graph of the height h, in meters above the edge of a cliff, against time t in seconds, for t from 0 to 8. The graph is a downward-opening parabola that starts at (0, -7), crosses the t-axis at t = 1, reaches its highest point at (4, 9), and then falls to (8, -7)." }) }] }] },
  "c5x-s44": { name: "Revenue and price", label: "Table", intro: String.raw`A store's weekly revenue $R(p)$, in dollars, depends on the price $p$, in dollars, it charges for a product. $R$ is twice differentiable and $R''(p) < 0$ for all $p$. Selected values of $R'(p)$ are given in the table below.`, sources: [{ title: "", blocks: [{ table: { head: [String.raw`$p$`, String.raw`$4$`, String.raw`$6$`, String.raw`$8$`, String.raw`$10$`, String.raw`$12$`], rows: [[String.raw`$R'(p)$`, String.raw`$2$`, String.raw`$-2$`, String.raw`$-7$`, String.raw`$-9$`, String.raw`$-12$`]] } }] }] },
